  "id": "genotypephenotype-correlation",
  "term": "genotype–phenotype correlation",
  "definition": "Genotype–phenotype correlation is the relationship between a genetic feature and the observable characteristics of a disorder. In this context, it means analyzing whether variation in genotype, such as repeat length, is associated with differences in clinical features like age at symptom onset or test findings.",
